--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS — IMPORTANT BEFORE SELLING
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This product is built on third-party frameworks whose licenses you MUST comply
with before any commercial distribution:

1. JUCE (https://juce.com)
   JUCE is dual-licensed. Open-source use falls under the AGPLv3; closed-source
   commercial distribution of a plugin requires a paid JUCE licence (or the
   applicable JUCE EULA tier). If you intend to SELL ApexAmp as closed source,
   you must obtain the appropriate JUCE licence first. See https://juce.com/get-juce

2. Steinberg ASIO SDK
   ASIO is a trademark and software of Steinberg Media Technologies GmbH. The ASIO
   SDK is used only to compile ASIO support; it is not redistributed in this
   repository. Distributing an ASIO-enabled product is subject to Steinberg's ASIO
   SDK Licensing Agreement, which you must accept/comply with.

3. VST3 SDK (bundled with JUCE)
   The VST3 format is a Steinberg technology under the Steinberg VST3 licence
   (GPLv3 or the proprietary Steinberg VST3 licence). Comply with its terms for
   commercial distribution.

4. Cabinet impulse responses (IRs)
   ApexAmp ships only its own original filter-based cab voicings. Any third-party
   IR files you load or distribute remain under their respective licences — do not
   bundle or redistribute commercial/copyrighted IRs without permission.

Bottom line: the ApexAmp code is yours, but obtain a JUCE commercial licence and
satisfy the Steinberg ASIO/VST3 terms before selling.
